  "semantics": {
    "inputLayout": "Exactly four lines: scalar n, exactly n a values, exactly n b values, scalar m. LF/CRLF accepted. No extra cases/lines.",
    "uniqueOutput": "One integer residue in [0,m). Non-interactive stdio; no floating/custom checker or multiple-valid-output construction.",
    "reasoning": "Nondecreasing x forces each x block to be contiguous in increasing order. A block of c points admits c! permutations except identical (x,i) copies. Each i occurs at most twice, and only a_i=b_i produces a multiplicity-two point. Divide each block by 2^d, where d is its count of equal-index pairs. Distinct blocks multiply.",
    "efficientOracle": "Counter groups by x; cancel denominator powers of two from integer factorial factors before modular multiplication. No modular inverse or post-reduction division. O(n) expected time and O(n) space.",
    "independentReferences": "Literal DFS enumerates distinct complete point sequences subject to nondecreasing x, without factorials or denominator counting. Separate reference inserts each distinct point multiplicity with binomial interleaving counts. Unit tests also use exact big-integer factorial quotient."
  },
